<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Fujian People's Government</h1><p class="st-meta">1933 CE – 1934 CE · capital Fuzhou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived rebel government in Fuzhou, set up in 1933 by the 19th Route Army in protest at Chiang Kai-shek's policy of appeasing Japan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/19th-route-army">19th Route Army</a>, famous for defending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1932, was moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> to fight the Communists. Its commanders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cai-tingkai">Cai Tingkai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiang-guangnai">Jiang Guangnai</a>, with the Nationalist dissidents <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jishen">Li Jishen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-mingshu">Chen Mingshu</a>, broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> and in November 1933 proclaimed the People's Revolutionary Government of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government rejected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>, adopted a new flag and a programme of resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, land reform and opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang</a>. It concluded a preliminary agreement with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chinese-soviet-republic">Chinese Soviet Republic</a>, but the Communist leadership gave no real military help, and other regional leaders also stayed aloof.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang</a> moved large forces against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>, and the rebellion collapsed in January 1934 after only two months. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/19th-route-army">19th Route Army</a> was broken up, and its leaders fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>, later joining the anti-Japanese struggle.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/fujian-peoples-government.jpg" alt="Fujian People's Government" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Froztbyte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Fujian_People%27s_Government.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1933 CE – 1934 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fuzhou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Li Jishen, Cai Tingkai, Chen Mingshu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Min Chinese, Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fujian People's Revolutionary Government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=fujian-peoples-government" aria-label="Fujian People's Government on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7831 1220 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Fujian People's Government lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8151 1476L8221 1549"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8221 1549h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8151 1476h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8151 1476h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fuzhou. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=fujian-peoples-government">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
